Z||000000||Alex2004||11-04-2001||11:24 PM||||Hi, on my 84 4cyl i've always had a slight oil leak coming from the push rod cover and now it's really bad, i was wondering how hard it is to take the cover off and change the gasket, also what all has to come off, and will i need to buy any other gaskets.  Thanks...<P>Alex...||||reg||4
Z||000001||maryjane||11-04-2001||11:32 PM||||You can change it without taking anything else off, but it is easier with the oil filter and the intake removed. Intake is really an optional removal. If you do take it off, mark all the hoses and wires WELL, and leave the TBI attached to it. Might be a good time to change out any brittle vacumn hoses as well. The studs that hold the cover on take little round sealing gaskets. Make sure you don't put the cover on upside down. Good luck<BR>Don <p>[This message has been edited by maryjane (edited 11-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tigger||11-04-2001||11:38 PM|||| <p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 11-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||BlackDragon||11-05-2001||12:10 AM||||i agree with mary. its not all that hard, im putting a new gasket on mine this week.<BR>of course mine will be a little easier to change cause it is on an engine stand, not in the car yet  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> but its still not that hard in the car<P>------------------<BR>civic sucks||||reg||1
